  "notes": "Modified cash basis governmental funds; business-type activities on accrual basis, so business_type uses net position from the proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses, and Changes in Net Position (p6), as in FY2023. Governmental receipts/disbursements from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4); fund balances printed (p4). Ending cash = Cash and cash equivalents 747,937 on the governmental funds balance sheet (p3); certificates of deposit 81,171 as ending_investments; county treasurer cash 7,554 printed separately (not added). No prior-year cash printed, so beginning_cash null. Transfers: Total column prints none (General in 3, Rehab out 3), so transfers_in/out null. Business-type receipts total computed (operating 403,228 + interest 54 + grant income 68,658); business-type 'Other revenue' 7,020 is counted in Charges for Services on the Statement of Activities (p2: 403,228). Grant income has no grantor printed (category other, detail Grants). Statement of Activities general-revenue page is not in the trim (only p2 expenses/program revenues). Balance sheet from the government-wide Statement of Net Position (governmental funds balance sheet excludes capital assets). General Fund detail from the departmental combining statement (p12), more detailed than the General Fund budget schedule (p8), which is not recorded to avoid double counting. Nonmajor funds (Rehab, Keno) recorded per fund from the combining statement (p11). Utility funds have no budget schedule; no business-type detail lines (as in FY2023/FY2024). Read pages 1-12 of 12"
}
